Auto-splines chunk-6 false-positive suppression on textured photos
==================================================================

Bench: 42 CID22-512/training photos × 2 distances (1.0, 2.0) × 2 efforts (e7, e8) = 168 cells.
Distance gate: existing chunk-3 trial-encode gate stays; chunk-6 adds an early
bbox-span gate that rejects any candidate whose bbox doesn't span the image's
long dimension.
Features: std parallel butteraugli-loop.
Harness: jxl-encoder/examples/auto_splines_chunk6_fp_bench.rs
Run host: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X / 128 GB / WSL2
Run date: 2026-05-17 UTC
Commit:   chunk-6 working commit (sibling workspace splines-chunk6-fp)

Photo corpus: /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/training/*.png
Sample selection: every 5th filename (sorted, skipping names with spaces);
                  first 42 → 42 distinct photos at 512×512 each.

Compares `LossyConfig::new(d).with_effort(e)` (auto_splines OFF)
against the same with `.with_auto_splines(true)`.

Chunk-6 change
--------------
File: jxl-encoder/src/vardct/splines.rs
- Added `detect_params::MIN_BBOX_SPAN_OF_IMAGE_LONG_DIM = 1.0`.
- In `spline_passes_trial_encode_gate`, an early-out is inserted
  before the existing trial-encode + energy-drop computation: any
  candidate whose bbox `max(w, h)` is below `MIN_BBOX_SPAN_OF_IMAGE_LONG_DIM
  * max(image_width, image_height)` is rejected. This is the chunk-6
  audit's "Option B" (ridge-length filter) realised at the candidate
  level instead of the polyline-trace level.

Rationale for the chosen option
-------------------------------
Options considered (from the A1 audit Top-5 #5 prompt):
  A. Raise Hessian eigenvalue ratio threshold (current 5) to 10.
     REJECTED: every observed FP already has high eigenvalue ratio
     (they are clean Sobel ridges, just on textured baselines).
  B. Add a ridge-length / bbox-span filter.                       SHIPPED.
  C. Per-block pre-classification by mask1x1.
     REJECTED: more compute (per-block) for the same effect; the
     bbox-span gate is cheaper and image-relative.
  D. (E&F internal alternatives) Raise COST_BENEFIT_MARGIN, add
     relative-energy-drop floor.
     REJECTED: the L2-energy proxy is dominated by the bbox's XYB
     DC term. Photo FPs and the chunk-3 stripe+ramp test image both
     sit in the same ~0.07-0.15 rel_drop band — no clean separator
     exists at any threshold. Lowering the floor enough to admit
     the test image leaves through half the FPs; raising it enough
     to catch all FPs kills the test image. An AC-only denominator
     was also implemented and discarded (still produced overlapping
     distributions).

Bbox span vs image long dim cleanly separates the two classes:
  Test image (1024×256 stripe+ramp + wire): bbox span 1024 = 1.0×.
  Photo FPs (all on 512×512): max bbox span 510 = 0.99× (some lower).

